; The parent of the orphan.  It delegates example. to ns.example. and
; carries an address for that name, because the name is below the
; delegation and so nothing else could: that is glue, and it is the only
; place the address exists.
;
; The child says the same name is its name server and then says nothing
; more about it.  So a resolver which keeps what the referral gave it
; can go on asking; one which takes the child's word for the NS RRset
; and looks the name up again has nowhere to look it up.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 3600
@		IN	SOA	ns.root. root.root. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@		IN	NS	ns.root.
ns.root.	IN	A	{{ROOT_ADDR}}
example.	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns.example.	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
example.	IN	DS	{{DS example}}
